{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Best card for a purchase"},"description":"Which credit card earns the most rewards for a purchase, and why. With no cards given and no saved wallet, it ranks every card earnrate knows (in `allCards`): a complete answer for anyone. With cards named in the conversation (`cards`) or a saved wallet, it picks the best of the user's own: `decision.cardId` is the pick and `decision.checkoutLabel` is how the card appears at checkout, with every usable card ranked with reasons, cards the merchant won't take, assumptions, warnings, and when a different point valuation would change the pick. For a business earnrate may not know, like a local restaurant, pass `category` when you can tell what kind of business it is. When the user is paying outside the U.S. or in another currency, pass `country`: abroad, each card is ranked after its foreign transaction fee. Pass `payment` only when the user says how they're paying, like Apple Pay or PayPal checkout. A statement credit (a card's `credit`, like Amex Platinum's lululemon credit) counts toward the pick only once it's enrolled in the wallet and has dollars left this period, and only when the amount is given; say its dollars apart from the % back. With no cards, `allCards.credits` lists cards with a credit at the store; present those first. Never needs or returns card numbers.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"amount":{"description":"Purchase amount in US dollars. Improves cap math.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"cards":{"description":"Cards the user named in this conversation, to answer for just those cards without saving anything. Leave out to use the user's saved wallet if they have one; with neither, the answer covers every card earnrate knows.","items":{"properties":{"activated":{"description":"Bonuses the user has activated with the issuer, as rule ids from search_cards.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"cardId":{"description":"A card id from search_cards.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"enrolled":{"description":"Statement credits the user has enrolled in with the issuer, and free nights they use, as ids from search_cards. A credit that needs enrolling counts only when it's here. Ask; never assume.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"opened":{"description":"The day the account opened (YYYY-MM-DD), for a card with a first-year rate. Optional; without it the card is ranked at its standard rates.","type":"string"},"picks":{"additionalProperties":{"items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"description":"Bonus categories the user picked, for cards that have them: choice id \u2192 option ids, from search_cards. Ask; don't guess.","propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"type":"object"},"skippedCredits":{"description":"Statement credit and free night ids the user says they don't use. They don't count toward a pick or against the card's annual fee.","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"required":["cardId"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"category":{"description":"Only for a merchant earnrate may not know, and only if you're confident what kind of business it is: its spending category, e.g. grocery.supermarket for a supermarket, dining for a restaurant, gas for a gas station. Ignored when earnrate knows the merchant. Leave it out if unsure. Categories: dining (Restaurants), dining.fast_food (Fast food), grocery.supermarket (Supermarkets), grocery.online (Online grocery and delivery), superstore (Superstores), warehouse_club (Warehouse clubs), convenience_store (Convenience stores), gas (Gas stations), gas.grocery_store (Gas at grocery stores), gas.superstore (Gas at superstores and warehouse clubs), ev_charging (EV charging), transit (Transit), transit.rideshare (Rideshare and taxis), travel (Travel), travel.flights (Flights), travel.hotels (Hotels), travel.car_rental (Car rentals), travel.cruise (Cruises), streaming (Streaming services), tv_internet (TV and internet service), phone (Cell phone service), utilities (Home utilities), housing (Rent and mortgage), drugstore (Drugstores and pharmacies), movie_theaters (Movie theaters), entertainment (Live entertainment and events), fitness (Gyms and fitness), department_store (Department stores), clothing (Clothing stores), electronics (Electronics stores), sporting_goods (Sporting goods stores), home_improvement (Home improvement), furniture (Furniture stores), online_retail (Online retail), office_supply (Office supply stores), shipping (Shipping and couriers), online_advertising (Social media and search advertising), other (Everything else).","enum":["dining","dining.fast_food","grocery.supermarket","grocery.online","superstore","warehouse_club","convenience_store","gas","gas.grocery_store","gas.superstore","ev_charging","transit","transit.rideshare","travel","travel.flights","travel.hotels","travel.car_rental","travel.cruise","streaming","tv_internet","phone","utilities","housing","drugstore","movie_theaters","entertainment","fitness","department_store","clothing","electronics","sporting_goods","home_improvement","furniture","online_retail","office_supply","shipping","online_advertising","other"],"type":"string"},"channel":{"description":"How the purchase is made. Omit if unknown; the answer says what it assumed.","enum":["online","in_store"],"type":"string"},"country":{"description":"Where the purchase is made, as a two-letter country code (FR, GB, JP). Pass it when the user is paying abroad or in another currency: abroad, cards are ranked after their foreign transaction fees. Default US.","pattern":"^[A-Za-z]{2}$","type":"string"},"date":{"description":"Purchase date, YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to today.","format":"date","pattern":"^(?:(?:\\d\\d[2468][048]|\\d\\d[13579][26]|\\d\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\\d|2[0-8])))$","type":"string"},"memberships":{"description":"Memberships the user has, such as amazon-prime or costco, when they're named in the conversation rather than saved.","items":{"enum":["amazon-prime","bank-of-america-account","bank-of-america-small-business-account","bofa-rewards-member","bofa-rewards-preferred-honors","bofa-rewards-preferred-plus","bofa-rewards-premier","caltech-efcu","costco","navy-federal","nordy-club-ambassador","penfed-honors-advantage","rei-co-op","sams-club","sams-club-plus","usbank-smartly-100","usbank-smartly-25","usbank-smartly-50","verizon-account"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"merchant":{"description":"Merchant name or web address as the user would say it or see it, e.g. \"Whole Foods\" or \"delta.com\", or a kind of place, e.g. \"restaurants\" or \"gas station\".","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"payment":{"description":"How the purchase is paid, only when the user says: card (the card itself or its number), apple-pay, google-pay or paypal (PayPal checkout). Optional; omit it when unknown, and never assume Apple Pay. Some rates need one (Apple Card's 2% with Apple Pay, PayPal Cashback's 3% through PayPal checkout), and the answer's assumptions say when paying another way would change the pick.","enum":["card","apple-pay","google-pay","paypal"],"type":"string"},"valuation":{"description":"Instead of the user's saved point values (or earnrate's defaults): flat, points at their cash-out value, MR and UR at 1\u00a2; or points-heavy, MR and UR at 1.7\u00a2, for people who transfer points to airlines and hotels.","enum":["flat","points-heavy"],"type":"string"}},"required":["merchant"],"type":"object"},"name":"best_card_for_purchase","outputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"allCards":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"assumptions":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"categoryNote":{"type":["string","null"]},"credits":{"items":